@startuml
!include ../../_style.iuml
' Derived from: crates/openmeet-core/src/types.rs (AnswerState, is_terminal, RequestKind, RequestSlot),
' crates/openmeet-engine/src/state.rs (answer_transition_allowed, AnswerStateMachine),
' crates/openmeet-engine/src/requests.rs (RequestManager::begin, set_state, cancel, cancel_all),
' crates/openmeet-engine/src/assist.rs (start_primary, run_primary, followups runner, background tasks),
' crates/openmeet-engine/src/screen.rs, crates/openmeet-engine/src/engine.rs (cancel_request, dismiss),
' src-tauri/src/commands/assistant.rs (cancel_request, dismiss_suggestion)
title AI request lifecycle - AnswerState (one AnswerStateMachine per RequestTicket)

hide empty description
left to right direction
skinparam StateFontSize 12

state "In flight (not is_terminal)" as InFlight {
  state Created : RequestManager::begin(slot, kind)\n/ emit AnswerStarted (Primary, Followups)
  state ContextBuilding : build_prompt_context
  state Requesting : LlmRequest sent\n(stream_text or complete)
  state Streaming : do / emit AnswerDelta (Primary),\nFollowupsReady { done: false } (Followups)

  [*] --> Created
  Created --> ContextBuilding : run_primary / followups runner
  Created --> Requesting : background tasks\n(Compression, Summary,\nQuestionClassification)
  ContextBuilding --> Requesting : context built\n[not ticket.is_cancelled()]
  Requesting --> Streaming : first delta
}

state Complete : emit AnswerComplete, Suggestion\nstored (Primary, Followups)
state Failed : error: Option<String>\n(user-facing message)
state Cancelled

Requesting --> Complete : Ok(text)\n(non-streamed result)
Streaming --> Complete : Ok(text)
InFlight --> Failed : Err(ProviderError)\nor no LLM provider (from Created)
InFlight --> Cancelled : ticket cancelled: begin() in same\nexclusive slot / cancel_request /\ndismiss_suggestion / cancel_all(..)\n/ ProviderError::Cancelled


note right of InFlight
  answer_transition_allowed(from, to):
  * from == to: accepted, nothing changes
  * from terminal: rejected (late states are ignored)
  * Failed / Cancelled: from any non-terminal state
  * ContextBuilding <- Created
  * Requesting <- Created | ContextBuilding
  * Streaming <- Requesting
  * Complete <- Requesting | Streaming
  * Created: never re-entered
end note

note bottom of Cancelled
  cancel_all(false): start_meeting, pause, stop_meeting (Background kept alive)
  cancel_all(true): emergency_stop (Background cancelled too)
  AnswerStateChanged { request_id, state, error } is emitted only for the
  Primary and Followups slots: while the ticket is current, and always
  for terminal states so the UI never hangs on a spinner.
end note

note left of Failed
  As implemented, TopicAnalysis and ScreenAnalysis
  call set_state(Complete) straight from Created;
  answer_transition_allowed rejects that move, so a
  successful run leaves the machine in Created
  (Failed / Cancelled still apply). TopicAnalysis
  reports a cancelled call as Failed.
end note
@enduml
